# Template for `.env` (which is GITIGNORED). Copy it and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This tool reads its PostHog session-access settings from this file whenever
# it invokes the PostHog CLI or fetches recording snapshots. These file values
# are the source of truth for provider access; shell credentials do not override them.

# --- REQUIRED FOR READING SESSIONS ---
# Personal API key for reading sessions via HogQL. This is a real secret — keep it out of version control.
# POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID=
# Query/API and recording-snapshot host. Optional; defaults to us.posthog.com.
# Set it for EU Cloud or a self-hosted domain:
# POSTHOG_API_HOST=eu.posthog.com
